## GitLab Orbit

[GitLab Orbit](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit): Give your agent a graph of your GitLab data and code, so the agent can answer questions about changes, pipelines, security, and code structure.

### Quickstart

[Quickstart](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/quickstart): Turn on GitLab Orbit for your group, connect your agent, and ask your first question about your merge requests, pipelines, and code.
[Start a free trial](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/trial): Start a free GitLab Orbit trial in a top-level group on GitLab.com, and find out what happens when the trial ends.

### Prompt examples

[Prompt examples](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/prompt-examples): Prompts to ask your agent about your code, merge requests, pipelines, deployments, and security with GitLab Orbit.

### Connect your agent

[Connect your agent](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/agents): Use GitLab Orbit in GitLab Duo, or connect any agent with the CLI or MCP.
[GitLab Orbit CLI](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/cli): Install the GitLab Orbit CLI, then query your GitLab data and code from the terminal.
[GitLab Duo](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/agents/duo): Use GitLab Orbit in GitLab Duo Agent Platform agents and flows to ground answers in your live GitLab data.
[GitLab Orbit MCP endpoint](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/agents/mcp): Connect MCP clients to GitLab Orbit with the GitLab Orbit MCP endpoint.

### GitLab Orbit dashboard

[GitLab Orbit dashboard](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/dashboard): Use the GitLab Orbit dashboard to check indexing, explore the schema, run queries, and manage which groups have GitLab Orbit turned on.

### Queries

[Queries](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/queries): Query the GitLab Orbit graph with GQL.
[Query language](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/queries/query-language): Query GitLab Orbit with GQL, a read-only, openCypher-like query language. Learn what GQL supports, the statement shape, filters, aggregations, pagination, and limits.

### GitLab Orbit architecture

[GitLab Orbit architecture](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/how-it-works): Learn how GitLab Orbit indexes your GitLab data and code, answers queries with your permissions, and keeps the graph current.
[Indexed data](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/schema): See which GitLab data and code GitLab Orbit indexes.
[Security](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/security): See how GitLab Orbit protects your data, and which roles you need.
[Glossary](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/glossary): Definitions of the terms used in the GitLab Orbit documentation.

### Troubleshooting

[Troubleshooting](https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/troubleshooting): Fix common errors in queries, the CLI, and the local graph.


